---
/**
 * /corporate-events/ — Corporate Events landing page.
 *
 * Audience-specific funnel split from /events. /events is the broad
 * group-events pillar; this page narrows to corporate planners (EA,
 * office manager, HR, owner) booking offsites, holiday parties,
 * staff appreciation nights, sales kickoffs, client entertainment.
 *
 * Per Context/seo.md (line 26): `corporate event venue near me` /
 * `team building venue` / `company outing bowling` is a $2K–$10K+
 * booking cluster, ~40% of paid corporate leads via Google. The
 * dedicated URL captures the planner-intent search that the broad
 * /events page dilutes (and competes against — same domain, blunter
 * keyword target).
 *
 * USE-CASE REFRAME (2026-06-16) — see
 * Context/session-handoffs/2026-06-16-corporate-events-usecase-reframe.md
 * The Google Ads "Events" campaign pivoted the corporate side away
 * from generic "event venue / event space" terms (wrong intent,
 * competed with banquet halls) toward high-intent USE-CASES: "team
 * outing," "staff outing," "employee appreciation," "company outing."
 * Paid traffic now arrives searching those phrases, so the page leads
 * with a use-case block that echoes the live ad-group copy ("Staff
 * Outings, Done Right," "Not Your Average Team Outing," "Reward Your
 * Team," "A Day They'll Remember") for keyword↔ad↔page scent
 * continuity (Quality Score + conversion). The VIP-suite + food/bar
 * editorial sections stay as the PROOF below the use-case grid.
 *
 * Replaces the legacy `/corporate-parties/` → `/events/#corporate`
 * 301 (hash drops on 301 so the equity was landing on the generic
 * events page). New redirect target: this page directly.
 *
 * Same pillar skeleton as /events + /fundraisers + /vip-suite (rule
 * of nine — .pillar-* CSS hoist is overdue, flagged on every page in
 * this family):
 *   - Hero: typography-led title section (no image)
 *   - Use-case grid: text-led "this is for YOU" blocks (the reframe)
 *   - Two long-scroll editorial sections (video + copy, alternating)
 *   - Closing CTA band → Plan an Event (PLAN_EVENT_URL toggle)
 *   - SnapFooter
 *
 * LCP note (changed in the 2026-06-16 reframe): the text-led use-case
 * grid now sits between the hero and the first video section, so the
 * vip-lanes poster is below the mobile fold and is NO LONGER the LCP
 * element — LCP is now hero/use-case TEXT (faster, no image to fetch).
 * Both section videos therefore use lazy `data-poster` and the page
 * passes NO `lcpPreloadHref` (a high-priority preload of a below-fold
 * poster is the exact waste-pattern the 2026-05-17 hero-preload fix
 * removed). If a future redesign moves a video back above the fold,
 * restore `poster=` + `lcpPreloadHref` on that one section.
 *
 * Hero videos: same as /vip-suite by user direction (2026-05-17) —
 * the VIP suite IS the corporate event room, so vip-lanes-* + buffet-*
 * is the visually correct pairing. Both videos are already canonical
 * on their primary pages (/vip-suite, /events) per src/data/videos.ts;
 * this page reuses them visually only and does NOT emit duplicate
 * VideoObject JSON-LD (single-canonical convention for the sitemap).
 *
 * Voice rules applied (per Context/voice.md):
 *   - Brian Van Flandern named only as "America's Top Mixologist"
 *     credential — "curated by," never "built by"
 *   - "private" hard-banned — VIP suite is "set apart from the main
 *     floor," "yours when you book it," "semi-private"
 *   - "Cheap / discount / value" banned — corporate planners have
 *     budgets, not coupons. Confident pricing language only.
 *   - "Team building" used pointedly (we're not running ropes-course
 *     activities; we're running an offsite that has bowling, food,
 *     and a real bar — the planner can call it team building)
 *   - Specifics > adjectives — 6-lane suite, up to 80, up to 200 for
 *     buyouts, 28 self-serve taps, LED video wall, near Naperville
 *
 * TODOs (non-blocking):
 *   - Capacity number for full-venue buyouts ("more for full-venue
 *     buyouts") still hand-waved; same as /events. When ops gives a
 *     number, update here + /events + /vip-suite in the same diff.
 *   - Real corporate-event photography (a real offsite night, a deck
 *     on the LED wall, a buffet from the kitchen at scale) would
 *     convert harder than the existing vip-lanes/buffet stock loops.
 *     Flagged for Context/media-needs.md.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SnapFooter from "../components/snap/SnapFooter.astro";
import BreadcrumbSchema from "../components/BreadcrumbSchema.astro";
import { BUSINESS_URL, BUSINESS_ENTITY_ID } from "../lib/schema";
import { ICON_PATHS } from "../lib/icons";

import { PLAN_EVENT_URL } from "../lib/links";

// JSON-LD: Service (parallel to /fundraisers). provider → #business
// links the program to the canonical entity via @id. areaServed is
// the I-55/I-80 corridor where corporate planners actually come from —
// Plainfield is the venue address, but the audience is anchored
// across the western suburbs (matches the /why-us/*-il/ city set).
const PAGE_URL = `${BUSINESS_URL}/corporate-events/`;
const serviceSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "@id": `${BUSINESS_URL}/#corporate-events`,
  name: "Corporate Events & Team Outings",
  url: PAGE_URL,
  description:
    "Team outings, staff outings, employee-appreciation nights, holiday parties, and corporate offsites at Twisted Pin in Plainfield, IL. Bowling in the 6-lane VIP suite (seats up to 80, or up to 200 for full-venue buyouts), in-house catering, and a cocktail program curated by Brian Van Flandern, America's Top Mixologist. Serving the I-55/I-80 corridor — Plainfield, Naperville, Bolingbrook, Joliet, Romeoville, Oswego, Shorewood, Lockport.",
  provider: { "@id": BUSINESS_ENTITY_ID },
  serviceType: "Corporate event & team outing hosting",
  areaServed: [
    { "@type": "City", name: "Plainfield, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Naperville, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Bolingbrook, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Joliet, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Romeoville, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Oswego, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Shorewood, IL" },
    { "@type": "City", name: "Lockport, IL" },
  ],
};

// FAQPage schema + on-page FAQ (2026-06-17, on-page SEO spec Phase A).
// Reuses the /faq accordion pattern — the t2-faq-* classes are global, and
// the Question/Answer JSON-LD shape matches /faq exactly. Questions are
// phrased the way a corporate planner actually searches (capacity, buyouts,
// catering, drink packages, distance) so the page answers the long-tail and
// feeds AI Overviews / ChatGPT / Perplexity. Answers honor the voice rules:
// "semi-private" (never "private"), "curated by" Brian, no chef-language, no
// discount framing, no fabricated drive times.
interface CorpFaq {
  q: string;
  /** Plain-text answer for JSON-LD (no HTML). */
  schemaA: string;
  /** Rendered HTML answer (may include <a> links). */
  htmlA: string;
}

const corpFaqs: CorpFaq[] = [
  {
    q: "Can you host a corporate event or team outing for 10–200 people near Naperville?",
    schemaA:
      "Yes. Twisted Pin in Plainfield — minutes from Naperville — hosts team outings, staff appreciation nights, holiday parties, and corporate offsites for groups from about 10 up to 200. The 6-lane VIP suite seats up to 80; full-venue buyouts handle up to 200.",
    htmlA: `<p>Yes. Twisted Pin in Plainfield — minutes from Naperville — hosts team outings, staff appreciation nights, holiday parties, and corporate offsites for groups from about <strong>10 up to 200</strong>. The <a href="/vip-suite/">6-lane VIP suite</a> seats up to 80; full-venue buyouts handle up to 200.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do you offer full-venue or VIP-suite buyouts for company events?",
    schemaA:
      "Both. Book the semi-private 6-lane VIP suite (up to 80, set apart from the main floor) for a single group, or buy out the whole venue for up to 200 when the entire company is coming.",
    htmlA: `<p>Both. Book the <strong>semi-private 6-lane VIP suite</strong> (up to 80, set apart from the main floor) for a single group, or <strong>buy out the whole venue</strong> for up to 200 when the entire company's coming.</p><p><a href="/vip-suite/">See the suite →</a></p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "What's included in the VIP suite for a corporate group?",
    schemaA:
      "Six dedicated lanes set apart from the main floor, an LED video wall with AV hookups for your deck or highlight reel, couch seating around the lanes, and direct access to the 28-tap self-serve beer and wine wall. In-house catering and the cocktail bar round it out.",
    htmlA: `<p>Six dedicated lanes set apart from the main floor, an <strong>LED video wall with AV hookups</strong> for your deck or highlight reel, couch seating around the lanes, and direct access to the 28-tap self-serve beer &amp; wine wall. In-house catering and the cocktail bar round it out.</p><p><a href="/vip-suite/">See the suite →</a></p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can you cater a company party, luncheon, or holiday party?",
    schemaA:
      "Yes — in-house catering through our kitchen, built to share and scaled to your group, served buffet or plated. Vegetarian, gluten-free, and other dietary accommodations on request. Works for an evening party or a daytime luncheon or training day.",
    htmlA: `<p>Yes — <a href="/eat/">in-house catering</a> through our kitchen, built to share and scaled to your group, served buffet or plated. Vegetarian, gluten-free, and other dietary accommodations on request. Works for an evening party or a daytime luncheon or training day.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do you offer drink packages or a bar for corporate events?",
    schemaA:
      "Yes. Run a tab, hand out drink tickets, or set a per-head cap — whichever fits the budget. The bar runs the cocktail program curated by Brian Van Flandern, America's Top Mixologist, plus the 28-tap self-serve beer and wine wall.",
    htmlA: `<p>Yes. Run a tab, hand out drink tickets, or set a per-head cap — whichever fits the budget. The bar runs the cocktail program <a href="/bar/">curated by Brian Van Flandern</a>, <em>America's Top Mixologist</em>, plus the 28-tap self-serve beer &amp; wine wall.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "How far is Twisted Pin from Naperville or Joliet?",
    schemaA:
      "We're in Plainfield at 15610 Joliet Rd — a short drive from both Naperville and Joliet, and central to Bolingbrook, Romeoville, Oswego, Shorewood, and Lockport. Free on-site parking.",
    htmlA: `<p>We're in Plainfield at <strong>15610 Joliet Rd</strong> — a short drive from both Naperville and Joliet, and central to Bolingbrook, Romeoville, Oswego, Shorewood, and Lockport. Free on-site parking.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "What's the minimum and maximum group size?",
    schemaA:
      "Corporate groups generally start around 10 and go up to 80 in the VIP suite, or up to 200 for a full-venue buyout. Tell us your headcount and we'll match the room to it.",
    htmlA: `<p>Corporate groups generally start around <strong>10</strong> and go up to <strong>80</strong> in the VIP suite, or up to <strong>200</strong> for a full-venue buyout. Tell us your headcount and we'll match the room to it.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can I plan an employee-appreciation event or team-building day here?",
    schemaA:
      "Absolutely — employee-appreciation nights, team-building outings, sales kickoffs, and holiday parties are exactly what the suite is for. No ropes course; just bowling, a real bar, and catering, set up for your group.",
    htmlA: `<p>Absolutely — employee-appreciation nights, team-building outings, sales kickoffs, and holiday parties are exactly what the suite is for. No ropes course; just bowling, a real bar, and catering, set up for your group.</p><p><a href="${PLAN_EVENT_URL}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Plan an event →</a></p>`,
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: corpFaqs.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.schemaA },
  })),
};
---
<Base
  title="Corporate Events & Team Outings in Plainfield, IL | Twisted Pin"
  description="Team outings, staff appreciation & holiday parties at Twisted Pin — minutes from Naperville. Bowling in the 6-lane VIP suite, cocktails & catering for 10–200."
  ogImage="/og/og-events.jpg"
  ogImageAlt="A corporate team outing in the 6-lane VIP suite at Twisted Pin in Plainfield, IL"
>

  {/* ============================================================
      HERO — typography-led title section (no image)

      Leads with the team-outing use-case (the new lead ad group).
      The H1 is a near-verbatim ad headline ("Not Your Average Team
      Outing") for maximal click→page scent. The sub packs the
      use-case cluster + proof points (suite, capacity, location).
      ============================================================ */}
  <section class="corp-hero" data-hero aria-labelledby="corp-hero-h1">
    <div class="corp-hero-copy">
      <p class="t-eyebrow hero-fade" data-delay-ms="0">Team Outings · Corporate Events</p>
      <h1 class="t-display corp-hero-headline hero-fade" id="corp-hero-h1" data-delay-ms="120">
        Not your average team&nbsp;outing.
      </h1>
      <p class="corp-hero-sub hero-fade" data-delay-ms="320">
        Staff outings, holiday parties, and employee-appreciation
        nights — bowling, craft cocktails, and catering in the 6-lane
        VIP suite. Groups of 10 to 200, minutes from Naperville.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================================
      USE-CASE GRID — the reframe. Text-led "this is for YOU" blocks,
      each echoing a live ad-group headline so paid traffic lands on
      copy that matches how they searched. No images = fast text LCP.
      The lead card (Team & Staff Outings) carries a "Most booked"
      tag + Glow border to signal "start here."
      ============================================================ */}
  <section class="corp-usecases" aria-labelledby="corp-uc-h2">
    <div class="corp-uc-head">
      <p class="t-eyebrow">What you're planning</p>
      <h2 class="t-display corp-uc-title" id="corp-uc-h2">
        One room. However your team runs it.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="corp-uc-grid">
      <li class="corp-uc-card corp-uc-card--lead">
        <span class="corp-uc-tag">Most booked</span>
        <p class="corp-uc-label">Team &amp; Staff Outings</p>
        <h3 class="corp-uc-headline">Staff outings, done right.</h3>
        <p class="corp-uc-body">
          Your own lanes, a real bar, and catering that isn't sad
          sandwiches in a conference room. The outing people actually
          clear their calendar for.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="corp-uc-card">
        <p class="corp-uc-label">Employee Appreciation</p>
        <h3 class="corp-uc-headline">Reward the team.</h3>
        <p class="corp-uc-body">
          Show the team you care — and mean it. Take over the suite
          for a day they'll remember, not another gift card buried in
          an inbox.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="corp-uc-card">
        <p class="corp-uc-label">Team Building</p>
        <h3 class="corp-uc-headline">Team building, minus the cringe.</h3>
        <p class="corp-uc-body">
          No trust falls, no ropes course. Just bowling, a little
          competition, and the kind of loose night where people
          actually talk. Call it team building — we won't argue.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="corp-uc-card">
        <p class="corp-uc-label">Company &amp; Holiday Parties</p>
        <h3 class="corp-uc-headline">The holiday party, handled.</h3>
        <p class="corp-uc-body">
          December books fast — lock the date by October. Full-venue
          buyouts for up to 200 when the whole company's coming.
        </p>
        <a class="corp-uc-link" href="/holiday-parties/">Holiday parties →</a>
      </li>

      <li class="corp-uc-card">
        <p class="corp-uc-label">Meetings &amp; Luncheons</p>
        <h3 class="corp-uc-headline">Daytime, when you need the room.</h3>
        <p class="corp-uc-body">
          A semi-private space with AV and catering for the lunch
          meeting, the training day, or the quarterly all-hands.
          Bowling optional.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="corp-uc-card">
        <p class="corp-uc-label">Fundraisers</p>
        <h3 class="corp-uc-headline">Fundraiser nights.</h3>
        <p class="corp-uc-body">
          Turn the lanes into a fundraiser — we'll help you structure
          the night so it actually pays off for the cause.
        </p>
        <a class="corp-uc-link" href="/fundraisers/">Fundraisers →</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="corp-uc-more">
      Planning something else? We also host <a href="/showers/">showers</a>,
      <a href="/wedding-receptions/">wedding receptions</a>, and
      <a href="/events/">all group events</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================================
      THE ROOM — image left, copy right (desktop). PROOF for the
      use-cases above. Below the mobile fold now (use-case grid sits
      above it), so the poster is lazy `data-poster` — NOT an LCP
      candidate. Bounded media on every <source>: ≤480 → 540w,
      ≥481 → 1080w (defense against the v.load() probing double-fetch).
      ============================================================ */}
  <section class="corp-section" aria-labelledby="corp-room-h2">
    <div class="corp-section-grid">
      <div class="corp-section-frame">
        <video
          class="corp-section-video"
          data-section-video
          preload="none"
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          data-poster="/snap/vip-lanes-poster.avif"
          aria-label="The 6-lane VIP suite at Twisted Pin — semi-private bowling lanes with LED video walls overhead, set up for a group event"
        >
          <source media="(max-width: 480px)" data-src="/snap/vip-lanes-mobile-av1-540.mp4"  type="video/mp4; codecs=av01.0.05M.08" />
          <source media="(max-width: 480px)" data-src="/snap/vip-lanes-mobile-h264-540.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <source media="(min-width: 481px)" data-src="/snap/vip-lanes-mobile-av1-1080.mp4"  type="video/mp4; codecs=av01.0.05M.08" />
          <source media="(min-width: 481px)" data-src="/snap/vip-lanes-mobile-h264-1080.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>
      <div class="corp-section-copy">
        <p class="t-eyebrow">The Room</p>
        <h2 class="t-display corp-section-title" id="corp-room-h2">
          Six lanes. Eighty people. Yours.
        </h2>
        <p class="corp-section-aside">(or up to 200 for full-venue buyouts)</p>

        <p class="corp-section-body">
          The <a href="/vip-suite/">6-lane VIP suite</a> sits behind a
          wall, set apart from the main floor — semi-private, yours
          for the night when you book it. LED video wall for the
          company deck, the highlight reel, the logo, or the playoff
          game once the meeting's over. AV solutions for the actual
          presentation if one has to happen.
        </p>

        <p class="corp-section-body">
          Couch seating wraps the lanes for the people who'd rather
          watch than throw. Run the all-hands at 6:30, call it the
          outing at 7, let the room handle the rest of the night.
        </p>

        <ul class="corp-section-list">
          <li>6-lane VIP suite, set apart from the main floor</li>
          <li>Up to 80 in the suite — or up to 200 for full-venue buyouts</li>
          <li>LED video wall + AV solutions for the deck</li>
          <li>Couch seating wraps the lanes</li>
          <li>Yours from setup to last call</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================================
      THE FOOD & BAR — image RIGHT, copy LEFT (alternation).
      Below the fold — lazy `data-poster`. Bounded media as above.
      ============================================================ */}
  <section class="corp-section corp-section--reverse" aria-labelledby="corp-food-h2">
    <div class="corp-section-grid">
      <div class="corp-section-frame">
        <video
          class="corp-section-video"
          data-section-video
          preload="none"
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          data-poster="/snap/buffet-poster.avif"
          aria-label="A buffet of catering food laid out for a group event at Twisted Pin — chafing dishes and shareable plates"
        >
          <source media="(max-width: 480px)" data-src="/snap/buffet-mobile-av1-540.mp4"  type="video/mp4; codecs=av01.0.05M.08" />
          <source media="(max-width: 480px)" data-src="/snap/buffet-mobile-h264-540.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <source media="(min-width: 481px)" data-src="/snap/buffet-mobile-av1-1080.mp4"  type="video/mp4; codecs=av01.0.05M.08" />
          <source media="(min-width: 481px)" data-src="/snap/buffet-mobile-h264-1080.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>
      <div class="corp-section-copy">
        <p class="t-eyebrow">The Food &amp; Bar</p>
        <h2 class="t-display corp-section-title" id="corp-food-h2">
          The kitchen and the bar handle the rest.
        </h2>

        <p class="corp-section-body">
          In-house catering through <a href="/eat/">the kitchen</a> —
          built to share, scaled to your group, served buffet or
          plated. Vegetarian, gluten-free, and dietary accommodations
          on request.
        </p>

        <p class="corp-section-body">
          The 28-tap self-serve <a href="/menu/taps/">beer &amp; wine
          wall</a> sits next door. The <a href="/menu/cocktails/">cocktail
          bar</a> runs the program curated by Brian Van Flandern,
          <em>America's Top Mixologist</em> — same drinks, same
          execution as the rest of the venue.
        </p>

        <p class="corp-section-body">
          Run a tab, hand out drink tickets, or set a per-head cap —
          pick the billing model that fits the budget. The kitchen
          handles custom catering through the night.
        </p>

        <ul class="corp-section-list">
          <li>In-house catering, buffet or plated</li>
          <li>28-tap self-serve beer &amp; wine wall</li>
          <li>Cocktail program curated by Brian Van Flandern</li>
          <li>Tab, drink tickets, or per-head cap — your call</li>
          <li>Dietary accommodations on request</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================================
      FAQ — search-phrased corporate Q&As. Reuses the global .t2-faq*
      accordion; emits FAQPage JSON-LD (see faqSchema in frontmatter).
      Sits above the closing CTA so the inquiry button stays the last
      beat on the page.
      ============================================================ */}
  <section class="corp-faq" aria-labelledby="corp-faq-h2">
    <div class="corp-faq-inner">
      <p class="t-eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="t-display corp-faq-title" id="corp-faq-h2">
        Corporate event FAQs.
      </h2>
      <div class="t2-faq">
        {corpFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="t2-faq-item">
            <summary class="t2-faq-q">
              <h3 class="t2-faq-q-text">{item.q}</h3>
              <svg
                class="t2-faq-chevron"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                width="18"
                height="18"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
                set:html={ICON_PATHS["chevron-down"]}
              />
            </summary>
            <div class="t2-faq-a" set:html={item.htmlA} />
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================================
      CLOSING CTA BAND — single dominant "Plan an event" → inquiry
      form (PLAN_EVENT_URL). This is THE conversion action (GA4
      generate_lead); the gclid-passthrough module decorates this
      href at runtime so ad-driven inquiries attribute back to Ads.
      Same lifted-indigo treatment as /events.
      ============================================================ */}
  <section class="corp-cta" aria-labelledby="corp-cta-h2">
    <div class="corp-cta-inner">
      <p class="t-eyebrow">Tell us what you need</p>
      <h2 class="t-display corp-cta-title" id="corp-cta-h2">
        We'll set it up.
      </h2>
      <p class="corp-cta-body">
        Plan your staff outing, company party, or appreciation night.
        Quick form — then a quote, a catering menu, and a tour of the
        suite.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-solid corp-cta-btn" href={PLAN_EVENT_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Plan an event
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SnapFooter />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(serviceSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  <BreadcrumbSchema crumbs={[
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Events", path: "/events/" },
    { name: "Corporate Events", path: "/corporate-events/" },
  ]} />
</Base>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     /corporate-events — same pillar skeleton as /events /vip-suite
     /fundraisers. Class names .corp-* mirror .events-* / .vip-* /
     .fundraiser-* — rule of nine, .pillar-* CSS hoist deeply overdue.
     Numbers match /events.astro byte-for-byte where applicable so
     the family reads cohesive across pages.
     ============================================================ */

